[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
mcp-grafana is installed but not enabled. To run it as a service:

  1. Create the environment file (mode 0600, root only) from the sample:
       cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/mcp_grafana.env.sample %%PREFIX%%/etc/mcp_grafana.env
     and set GRAFANA_URL. Set MCP_GRAFANA_SERVER_TOKEN to require a bearer
     token from clients.

  2. Enable and configure it in /etc/rc.conf:
       mcp_grafana_enable="YES"
       mcp_grafana_address="0.0.0.0:8443"
       mcp_grafana_allowed_hosts="mcp.example.com:8443"
       mcp_grafana_tls_cert="/path/to/fullchain.pem"
       mcp_grafana_tls_key="/path/to/key.pem"

  3. service mcp_grafana start

The server only accepts loopback Host names unless mcp_grafana_allowed_hosts
is set, and it serves plain HTTP unless both TLS files are given. Clients
send their Grafana token in X-Grafana-Service-Account-Token.
EOM
}
]
